Test canvases for every viewer (issue 202).

Each NN-name.canvas is a canvas as viewers receive it (docs/canvas-protocol.md),
and NN-name.expected is what the viewer-side reader (src/022-viewer.lua)
gives for it. Each viewer (the Lua window, the terminal view, the HTML page,
the Android and watch apps) is checked against the same pairs, so they all
agree on what a canvas says.

An .expected file, one item a line, after a # comment line:

    version N                    the canvas's version
    size WxH                     its size in characters
    voices NAME NAME ...         the voices header, in colour order
    cell ROW COLUMN CODEPOINT    every cell, in reading order: its character
                                 as a decimal Unicode code point (32 is a space)
         ... VOICE VERSION KIND AGE
                                 and, when it has one, its mark and the mark's
                                 age (the canvas version minus the mark's)
    previous NAME|none           the version the viewer drew before
    changed ROW COLUMN WAS NOW   each cell whose character differs from it,
                                 code points; WAS is - when there is no
                                 previous version (then every cell that is
                                 not a space is listed)
    refused LINE                 instead of all the above: the canvas must be
                                 refused, naming this line number

02 and 03 are the kitten and dog example of docs/datapath-blit.md, made by
the real change finder, blit and marks; 04 has marks of several ages, an
orphan, a mark by kuvalu and two-byte characters; 05 and 06 must be
refused. The .expected files were written from the reader's answers and
checked by hand, cell by cell; src/023-test-viewer.lua holds the reader to
them.
